module {{.Module}}

go 1.26.4

// The Go this app is built with, which to begin with is payday's: the
// toolchain payday is built and tested with. setup-go's go-version-file reads
// this line, and a go command older than it fetches it (GOTOOLCHAIN=auto).
//
// It is written here because nothing else writes it. `go get -tool` raises the
// go line above to payday's and adds no toolchain, and an app with none is
// built with exactly what its go line names -- go1.27.0 when levyan was made,
// whose standard library govulncheck had advisories against (payday#189).
// From here on it is the app's, and Renovate moves it.
toolchain go1.27.3

// The generators, as tools of this module.
//
// They are pinned here rather than by payday because a plugin is a Go program
// built from **this** module's graph -- so its version is this app's to choose,
// and `pd doctor` is what says when one is missing rather than `buf generate`
// failing over an executable nobody has heard of.
//
// `go mod tidy` fills in the requires. Nothing but the toolchain is pinned in
// this file, on purpose: a template that carried version numbers would be a
// template that is out of date the week after it was written. The toolchain is
// not, because it is payday's own and moves when payday's does.
tool (
	github.com/protobuf-orm/ent/cmd/ent
	github.com/lesomnus/payday/cmd/pd
	github.com/lesomnus/payday/cmd/protoc-gen-pd
	github.com/protobuf-orm/protobuf-merge
	github.com/protobuf-orm/protoc-gen-orm-ent
	github.com/protobuf-orm/protoc-gen-orm-go
	github.com/protobuf-orm/protoc-gen-orm-service
	google.golang.org/grpc/cmd/protoc-gen-go-grpc
	google.golang.org/protobuf/cmd/protoc-gen-go
)
